I received a mail from:

  Date:    Sat, 15 Jun 1996 22:46:20 -0400
  From:    Gyula Szokoly <szgyula@skysrv.Pha.Jhu.EDU>
  Subject: Re: Disktab entry for HP C3725S

for my difficulty. Thanks, Gyula.
As a result, the disktab entry for "HP C3725S" is not necessary.
Instead the following command can write the geometry info into
the disk.

  disklabel -wr rz5 rzXX

In my case, "disklabel -wr rz3 rz3" went fine.

Here is my original question,
-------------------------- from here ---------------------------
I bought a disk called "HP C3725S" and connected to my machine
(DECpc AXP150 running OSF/1 V2.0) physically. But there is no
entry for the disk in my /etc/disktab. Does anybody have the
entry of disktab for "HP C3725S" including the sample definition
of the partitions ? I've found the following entry on a web called
"CMI" ( or something like that ):

              HP_C3725S_noswap:\
                        :No swap or boot:ns#125:nt#9:nc#1864:\
                        :s0#2097000:b0#8192:f0#1024:\
                        :se#1024:rm#5400:

but it seems not to have enough info to use, and I don't know
whether the above entry can be used on my machine or not.
---------------------------- to here ----------------------------

and Gyula's suggestion.
---------------------------- from here ---------------------------
> I bought a disk called "HP C3725S" and connected to my machine
> (DECpc AXP150 running OSF/1 V2.0) physically. But there is no
> entry for the disk in my /etc/disktab. Does anybody have the
> entry of disktab for "HP C3725S" including the sample definition
> of the partitions ? I've found the following entry on a web called
> "CMI" ( or something like that ):

  What happens if you just let the OS figure it out?

disklabel -wr rz5 rzXX

(change rz5 to the right SCSI id, and keep the 'rzXX' -- it means go and
figure it out). You can also get out geometry info with the 'scu' utility.
