From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Jun 13 13:35:01 1996
From: Christian Bonhomme <cb () www ! web-data ! fr>
Date: Thu, 13 Jun 1996 13:35:01 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: xtrlock vs dxpause
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076333621351

I change xtrlock code to work in C2 security.
Why do i use xtrlock ?

* dxpause can be killed on PC with X emulation (Qvision, eXceed, ..)
	if you click very fast on the 'OK' bouton

* dxpause lock all X events, and some X terminals reset their
	connections or X11 server (you have to change a delay somewhere)

* dxpause doesn't let you to see what's on the screen

* xtrlock works on almost all systems even in C2 security

* 'root' password unlock the screen too (dxpause NOT)

* xtrlock memory usage is smaller.


you can get xtrlock <URL:ftp://www.web-data.fr/pub/>


