To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Configuring HSZ40
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076333621326

Vince,

	You may want to try serveral different things:

	1. I don't specify the letter "a" in the /sys/conf/MACHINE file

	Change:
	device disk     rza8      at scsi1     drive     64
	...

	For:
	device disk     rz8      at scsi1     drive     64
	...

	2. I have configured two systems with Storage Works and I had to consider
	the HSZ as having SCSI ID 2 instead of 1. Therefore you would have devices
	rza16, rzb16 .... It seems that the HSZ40 "adds" one to the physical SCSI 
	ID which is 1.

	Regards,

	Pedro

