I summarized:

> >> I'm installing the Tripwire 1.2 package, and wondered if anybody had a
> >> generic configuration file they'd like to share?
> >
> >The silence was deafening.  I got one reply asking for me to summarize,
> >or post my own config file.
> >
> >Meanwhile, I've run into compiler warnings, and can't get tripwire to pass
> >its own tests.  Maybe nobody else has gotten it working on DU 3.2B?

Two guys, specifically Guy Evans <Guy.Evans@brunel.ac.uk> and Guy Helmer
<ghelmer@alpha.dsu.edu> sent me some more information.

Guy Evans wrote:
> 
> Don't worry about the tests failing.  If I remember rightly the tests
> assume that enough time passes between certain code branches that the
> modified stamp of the test file will be different.  On the alpha it is not.
> 
> CHeers
> GUy

I was able to confirm this.  The standard test scripts have sleep statements
that are disabled with comments about a bug with SunOS tmpfs.  When I enabled
these sleep statements, tripwire passed all its tests.

Guy Helmer sent me his tripwire config file, which I'm adapting to one of our
servers here at SPU.

Also, Tim Mooney <mooney@toons.cc.ndsu.NoDak.edu> is working on a "new-and-
improved" tripwire config for a DU 3.2D host, and suggested we could do some
stepwise refinement on it once he's got it working the way he wants it.

I've placed a copy of my current config file on the World Wide Web at this
URL:
	http://paul.spu.edu/~prand/tripwire/tw.config_noah.spu.edu

It's definitely a work in progress, but have a look if you're interested.

If others are interested in working on a generic Digital Unix tripwire 
configuration file, I'm willing to act as the clearinghouse.

