Actually, in regard to alan@nabeth remarks below.  Here is what I do
and
works great.

        (1) Filesystems are within AdvFS domains.

        (2) Add new disk, create LSM volumes using whole disk or
        subdisks as desired.

        (3) Add new LSM volumes to existing AdvFS domain and presto
        all filesystems in that AdvFS domain now have that amount
        of additional space free.

        With AdvFS, the filesystems can automatically use (growby)
        the amount of new space added to the AdvFS domain.  Since,
        it is easy to add new space to domains on-line, this is
        my preferred method of handling the issue.

        AdvFS addvol and rmvol commands are beautiful things.

        Regards/Bob Reinhardt

