     From: alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com
     
     Neither UFS nor AdvFS automatically grow the file system to fill
newly 
     available space.  As it turns out there still aren't utilities
that 
     can grow the file system offline or online to use newly
available 
     space.  I've heard rumors of plans for such a utility for AdvFS,
but 
     it has been a consisently less desirable feature than such
things as 
     MP friendlyness and not panicing the system in the face of an
I/O 
     error.  I think OSF provides such a utility for UFS in their 
     distribution, but we didn't include in Digital UNIX.
     
     The only solution is to backup, re-create the file system and
restore.
      Please make your dissatisfaction known to the CSC, so they can
make
     it known to the engineering groups.
     
